      },
      "text": "d",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.635700232241334,
        "y0": 0.3688518191176752,
        "x1": 0.653448281167936,
        "y1": 0.3795007266228103
      },
      "text": ", R",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6534483837480305,
        "y0": 0.3678410783799414,
        "x1": 0.6643391585149685,
        "y1": 0.37494034212162264
      },
      "text": "m",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.665347674714417,
        "y0": 0.3688518191176752,
        "x1": 0.8869958188353466,
        "y1": 0.3795007266228103
      },
      "text": "). By linking m-multiwavelets to",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11334659352022058,
        "y0": 0.38182081122862754,
        "x1": 0.8869949981945904,
        "y1": 0.3924697187337626
      },
      "text": "vector-valued wavelets, our approach not only enables the systematic construction of separable multivariate bases",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11334656787519695,
        "y0": 0.39479027451358895,
        "x1": 0.14823753292821035,
        "y1": 0.405439182018724
      },
      "text": "in L²",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14904438948430934,
        "y0": 0.39479027451358895,
        "x1": 0.1659855690323004,
        "y1": 0.405439182018724
      },
      "text": "(R",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1659856972574186,
        "y0": 0.39377906260184603,
        "x1": 0.17243947261521797,
        "y1": 0.40087832634352727
      },
      "text": "d",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1732460727210806,
        "y0": 0.39479027451358895,
        "x1": 0.19119566588842568,
        "y1": 0.405439182018724
      },
      "text": ", R",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19119578129103204,
        "y0": 0.39377906260184603,
        "x1": 0.20208654323545824,
        "y1": 0.40087832634352727
      },
      "text": "m",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20289287406857273,
        "y0": 0.39479027451358895,
        "x1": 0.8873970224075959,
        "y1": 0.405439182018724
      },
      "text": ") that satisfy the vector-valued multiresolution analysis but also ensures that these bases inherit key",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11334664481026786,
        "y0": 0.4077592666245413,
        "x1": 0.6056489832261029,
        "y1": 0.41840817412967635
      },
      "text": "structural properties, making them well-suited for practical applications.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09660883029969801,
        "y0": 0.42795373255170155,
        "x1": 0.929143235663406,
        "y1": 0.43978584633870255
      },
      "text": "Key words : Multivariate wavelet bases; Vector-valued wavelet bases; Vector-valued multiresolution decomposi-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.0713982590106355,
        "y0": 0.4422055140243857,
        "x1": 0.38198247316504724,
        "y1": 0.45403762781138657
      },
      "text": "tion; m-multiwavelets; Separable wavelets.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.4760493813104697,
        "x1": 0.08494889075014772,
        "y1": 0.49308762357806935
      },
      "text": "1",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11213746912339155,
        "y0": 0.4760493813104697,
        "x1": 0.26138092810366337,
        "y1": 0.49308762357806935
      },
      "text": "Introduction",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.5071935302571277,
        "x1": 0.9291417738970589,
        "y1": 0.5190256440441285
      },
      "text": "Since the 1990s, wavelets have gained significant attention in signal processing and data analysis due to their ability",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.5214453117298117,
        "x1": 0.9293409844406513,
        "y1": 0.5332774255168127
      },
      "text": "to capture both frequency and time-domain information simultaneously. This dual capability makes them particularly",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.5355546899192973,
        "x1": 0.9293454979648109,
        "y1": 0.5473868037062983
      },
      "text": "well-suited for analyzing non-stationary signals. Wavelets have become a standard theoretical framework for analyzing",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.5498064713919815,
        "x1": 0.9291411584164916,
        "y1": 0.5616385851789824
      },
      "text": "signals [2], processes [21], and multifractal functions [22]. A fundamental concept in this framework is multiresolution",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.563915849581467,
        "x1": 0.8234621192226891,
        "y1": 0.5757479633684679
      },
      "text": "decomposition (MRA), which enables the representation of a function at different levels of resolution.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8323362206210609,
        "y0": 0.563915849581467,
        "x1": 0.9291427996980042,
        "y1": 0.5757479633684679
      },
      "text": "By capturing",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.578167631054151,
        "x1": 0.9291445435596113,
        "y1": 0.589999744841152
      },
      "text": "local and global information, wavelets provide a flexible tool for tasks ranging from function approximation to data",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.5924194125268352,
        "x1": 0.4402690470719538,
        "y1": 0.6042515263138362
      },
      "text": "compression and reconstruction from samples [1].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.45236975405396534,
        "y0": 0.5924194125268352,
        "x1": 0.9291405429359244,
        "y1": 0.6042515263138362
      },
      "text": "This versatility has revolutionized the analysis of functions and",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.6065283195423117,
        "x1": 0.5519962086397059,
        "y1": 0.6183604333293127
      },
      "text": "signals in theoretical mathematics and engineering applications.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5653073094472164,
        "y0": 0.6065283195423117,
        "x1": 0.928944204634979,
        "y1": 0.6183604333293127
      },
      "text": "The origins of wavelets date back to 1909 when",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.6207801010149958,
        "x1": 0.7809095879562763,
        "y1": 0.6326122148019968
      },
      "text": "Alfred Haar introduced the first wavelet basis [30], long before the term ”wavelet” was coined.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7920021890592175,
        "y0": 0.6207801010149958,
        "x1": 0.9293452928046219,
        "y1": 0.6326122148019968
      },
      "text": "The Haar wavelet,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.6350318824876799,
        "x1": 0.808136755678834,
        "y1": 0.6468639962746808
      },
      "text": "while simple and orthogonal, is discontinuous, limiting its applicability in some practical contexts.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8194305676372111,
        "y0": 0.6350318824876799,
        "x1": 0.9291444409795168,
        "y1": 0.6468639962746808
      },
      "text": "However, Haar",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.6491412606771655,
        "x1": 0.5352592917049632,
        "y1": 0.6609733744641664
      },
      "text": "wavelets have proven useful in various theoretical contexts [29].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09660844562434348,
        "y0": 0.6633930421498495,
        "x1": 0.9289419478728992,
        "y1": 0.6752251559368505
      },
      "text": "Significant advances in wavelet theory were achieved in the 1980s, notably by Yves Meyer [31] and Ingrid Daubechies",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.6775024203393352,
        "x1": 0.9289416401326156,
        "y1": 0.6893345341263362
      },
      "text": "[16]. Meyer’s wavelets are constructed using a band-limited function, ensuring smoothness and regularity in the time",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": null,
      "text": "arXiv:2503.04255v1  [math.FA]  6 Mar 2025",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.6917542018120193,
        "x1": 0.9291431074382878,
        "y1": 0.7035863155990202
      },
      "text": "domain. Although they lack compact support, their smoothness and orthogonality make them suitable for applications",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.7060059832847033,
        "x1": 0.4088058087004333,
        "y1": 0.7178380970717042
      },
      "text": "requiring continuously differentiable wavelets.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4186882980731355,
        "y0": 0.7060059832847033,
        "x1": 0.9291473132221638,
        "y1": 0.7178380970717042
      },
      "text": "In contrast, Daubechies wavelets are constructed to possess compact",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.7201153614741889,
        "x1": 0.16317918280593488,
        "y1": 0.7319474752611899
      },
      "text": "support and",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1716340650029543,
        "y0": 0.7201153614741889,
        "x1": 0.250102426224396,
        "y1": 0.7319474752611899
      },
      "text": "a specified",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.25855769309676996,
        "y0": 0.7201153614741889,
        "x1": 0.31391196371126573,
        "y1": 0.7319474752611899
      },
      "text": "number",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3222893210018382,
        "y0": 0.7201153614741889,
        "x1": 0.4912960276884191,
        "y1": 0.7319474752611899
      },
      "text": "of vanishing moments.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5070269929260767,
        "y0": 0.7201153614741889,
        "x1": 0.928941537552521,
        "y1": 0.7319474752611899
      },
      "text": "These properties enhance localization and facilitate the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.734367142946873,
        "x1": 0.33821898388261556,
        "y1": 0.746199256733874
      },
      "text": "approximation of smooth functions.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.35132846351431196,
        "y0": 0.734367142946873,
        "x1": 0.9291402351956407,
        "y1": 0.746199256733874
      },
      "text": "A key advantage of Daubechies wavelets is their ability to combine compact",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.7486189244195571,
        "x1": 0.9293447799041492,
        "y1": 0.760451038206558
      },
      "text": "support with adjustable vanishing moments, making them particularly effective for smooth function approximation,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.7627283026090427,
        "x1": 0.9291427996980042,
        "y1": 0.7745604163960437
      },
      "text": "signal analysis, and image processing [16, 39, 38]. The vanishing moments of the Daubechies wavelets play a crucial role",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.7769800840817268,
        "x1": 0.9291430048581932,
        "y1": 0.7888121978687277
      },
      "text": "in the multifractal formalism. More precisely, they make the wavelets orthogonal to low-order polynomials, enabling",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.7910889910972033,
        "x1": 0.9291436203387605,
        "y1": 0.8029211048842042
      },
      "text": "the removal of such trends. Sequentially, wavelet transforms based on Daubechies wavelets characterize H¨older spaces",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.8053407725698875,
        "x1": 0.9289396911108193,
        "y1": 0.8171728863568883
      },
      "text": "and pointwise regularity. They allow estimating the H¨older exponent through decay conditions in wavelet leaders [3].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09660844562434348,
        "y0": 0.8195925540425715,
        "x1": 0.9287396599264706,
        "y1": 0.8314246678295725
      },
      "text": "Yves Meyer’s pioneering work on wavelets laid the foundation for St´ephane Mallat’s multiresolution analysis (MRA)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.8337019322320571,
        "x1": 0.20490917558429622,
        "y1": 0.845534046019058
      },
      "text": "in the scalar case.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2149932091977416,
        "y0": 0.8337019322320571,
        "x1": 0.9291454667804622,
        "y1": 0.845534046019058
      },
      "text": "MRA provides a systematic and theoretical framework for constructing wavelet bases for spaces",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07139836159073004,
        "y0": 0.8479537137047413,
        "x1": 0.15227187982126444,
        "y1": 0.8597858274917421
      },
      "text": "such as L²",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1530789928275998,
        "y0": 0.8479537137047413,
        "x1": 0.1827252043395483,
        "y1": 0.8597858274917421
      },
      "text": "(R).",
